# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: keyak-keccakp-prototype
why: KeccakF-interface.h maps KeccakF_StatePermute to KeccakP1600_12_StatePermute but does not include
why: KeccakP-1600-12-interface.h, which declares it; SerialFallback.c then calls it with no prototype
why: in scope (C89 implicit `int f()`), while KeccakP-1600-12-reference.c defines it `void f(void *)`.
why: Native ABIs ignore the mismatch; WebAssembly checks call signatures, and the linker replaces the
why: call with a trap (invalid code in KeccakF_ParallelStatePermute, CI run 45393949691). The patch
why: adds the declaration from KeccakP-1600-12-interface.h (identical) in front of the first function
why: of SerialFallback.c. No code changes.
file: upstream/SerialFallback.c
count: 1
find: void KeccakF_ParallelInitialize( void )
replace: void KeccakP1600_12_StatePermute(void *state); void KeccakF_ParallelInitialize( void )
